{"data": [{"author_id": "1499198533106540546", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:05:52.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117422980355830192"], "id": "2117422980355830192", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117075900575477855", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ Best model scores 12%. Finally, a benchmark that makes AI feel the way I felt about calculus.", "url": "https://x.com/ajutqs/status/2117422980355830192"}, {"author_id": "2084657997519941632", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:05:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117422877381362132"], "id": "2117422877381362132", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117075900575477855", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ If you put the model size next to each of these models and sort by size the chart like pretty much stays the same...", "url": "https://x.com/covrov0/status/2117422877381362132"}, {"author_id": "1798677894027497472", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:53:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117419916387401907"], "id": "2117419916387401907", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117075900575477855", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ Where is your mea culpa after your big claim that Google will never have SOTA models again?? Without intellectual honesty (most important aspect is admitting when you are wrong) a research firm has no foundations", "url": "https://x.com/heximan64627/status/2117419916387401907"}, {"author_id": "502329359", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:38:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117416135792767315"], "id": "2117416135792767315", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117075900575477855", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ 12% on real expert tasks is the useful headline. Curious how much of that gap is refusal vs failed execution once the agent is allowed to keep going.", "url": "https://x.com/idooing/status/2117416135792767315"}, {"author_id": "517916836", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:32:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117414514245120366"], "id": "2117414514245120366", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 22, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117075900575477855", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ Thanks for sharing! I noticed no healthcare domain tasks, do you need a partner for that?", "url": "https://x.com/TurkMatthew/status/2117414514245120366"}, {"author_id": "2112837593888882688", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:26:11.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117412990303560140"], "id": "2117412990303560140", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117075900575477855", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ 12% at the top is the real headline. GDPx finally scores actual work, not exams—agents still fail most of the job.", "url": "https://x.com/laoxiongdgj/status/2117412990303560140"}, {"author_id": "2109669900059070464", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:09:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117408746595107207"], "id": "2117408746595107207", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117075900575477855", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ 最强才 12% 有点意外。想问下失败主要卡在哪一步：找不到文件、长时间跑偏，还是最后交付质量不过关？", "url": "https://x.com/Kaixin01234/status/2117408746595107207"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:46:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117402905867092269"], "id": "2117402905867092269", "in_reply_to_user_id": "806144160436809728", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117402764938756446", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@msdkhairi @SemiAnalysis_ The $16.29/task for Gemini 4 Carbon uses the standard API rates ($4 input / $20 output per 1M tokens), not the temporary intro pricing ($2/$10). \n\nThat matches the 594K output tokens roughly (output alone ~$11.88 at $20/M, plus input). Artificial Analysis and similar trackers", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2117402905867092269"}, {"author_id": "806144160436809728", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:45:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117402764938756446"], "id": "2117402764938756446", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 13, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117075900575477855", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ @grok The cost of Carbon is the actual api pricing or the temporary introductory pricing?", "url": "https://x.com/msdkhairi/status/2117402764938756446"}, {"author_id": "2065701479760134148", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:40:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117401406089117791"], "id": "2117401406089117791", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117075900575477855", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ The git-lfs example is brutal: a patch can fix the error and still break the fetch budget. 'Does the new thing work?' is only half the test. 'What did we accidentally change?' is the other half.", "url": "https://x.com/098uyiubgvgcss/status/2117401406089117791"}, {"author_id": "2075185310938390528", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:58:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117391038213980244"], "id": "2117391038213980244", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117075900575477855", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ Con 3 preguntas se consumen los tokens de Argón siendo más económico que carbón , opus 5.5 me permite un cupo mucho más extenso , no sé cómo hacen sus comparativas de precios", "url": "https://x.com/Afirezant/status/2117391038213980244"}, {"author_id": "1963002119918620672", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:45:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117387646364242341"], "id": "2117387646364242341", "in_reply_to_user_id": "471997769", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117204917144170915", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlphaMFPEFM @damaonx @SemiAnalysis_ Thanks. Sorry my bad!", "url": "https://x.com/Balabo111/status/2117387646364242341"}, {"author_id": "1571930270898556930", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:37:11.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117385562294517988"], "id": "2117385562294517988", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117075900575477855", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ the safety classifier point is underrated. for anyone choosing a model at work, refusals can matter more than raw capability.\n\ncurious how many of the finance and legal 0s were near misses vs total fails.", "url": "https://x.com/5pmHQ/status/2117385562294517988"}, {"author_id": "72022803", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:07:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117378105165942947"], "id": "2117378105165942947", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 23, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117075900575477855", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ 12% at the top is useful. A benchmark everyone already scores 90% on can't tell you much about the next model. Up to 8 hours per task in a real deal room is also much closer to what a new hire actually gets handed. I'd love to see how the scores move if the agent is allowed to", "url": "https://x.com/mikejt4/status/2117378105165942947"}, {"author_id": "2059896543264550914", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:50:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117373760798175480"], "id": "2117373760798175480", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 17, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117075900575477855", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ Detail from the write-up: Opus 5.5 and GPT-6 Astra lose points when their own safety classifiers block cyber, biology and alignment tasks, so you also publish a ranking with those three domains left out.", "url": "https://x.com/Telasian/status/2117373760798175480"}, {"author_id": "420308365", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:24:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117367391479005532"], "id": "2117367391479005532", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 291, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117075902865531210", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ @chakra_ai mentioned", "url": "https://x.com/nic_carter/status/2117367391479005532"}, {"author_id": "2085838061347217408", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:20:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117366142410887419"], "id": "2117366142410887419", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1322190427", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 41, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117366111402639611", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AnthonyKoochew @SemiAnalysis_ On it, sending this to your Grok Bot now. It'll take it from here.", "url": "https://x.com/bot/status/2117366142410887419"}, {"author_id": "1322190427", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:19:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117366111402639611"], "id": "2117366111402639611", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 10, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117075900575477855", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ @bot give the details to Clive for the research app", "url": "https://x.com/AnthonyKoochew/status/2117366111402639611"}, {"author_id": "2110846617033363456", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:47:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117358003162886331"], "id": "2117358003162886331", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117075900575477855", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ Running each model in its own native harness, like Claude Code for Opus and Codex for Astra, is closer to how people actually use them. Would love a run with every model in one shared harness too, to separate model gains from harness gains.", "url": "https://x.com/aitrendster/status/2117358003162886331"}, {"author_id": "239549060", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:18:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117350571766104571"], "id": "2117350571766104571", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117075900575477855", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ Best model at 12% is only meaningful if the task set is well-defined and the scoring is reproducible. 1/7 doesn't tell me much until I know the sample size and whether contamination was ruled out. 🔍", "url": "https://x.com/ledgerdetective/status/2117350571766104571"}, {"author_id": "72918669", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:46:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117327451680358646"], "id": "2117327451680358646", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117075900575477855", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ best model at 12% on agentic tasks. honestly that matches what I see at home, the agent loops fine for 5 min then quietly does something dumb.", "url": "https://x.com/TULIOANDREZO/status/2117327451680358646"}, {"author_id": "261185971", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:22:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117321371751727448"], "id": "2117321371751727448", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 146, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117075911379923377", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ @ARCVEREX @ariadata_ @nratliff9 @arithmeticlabs1 @uri_rolls @btfl_machines @akarshaurora @chakra_ai @27upon2 @datacurve What exactly is a 100% a super god?", "url": "https://x.com/mariusschober/status/2117321371751727448"}, {"author_id": "1463820099446525956", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:10:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117318565300961615"], "id": "2117318565300961615", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 16, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117075900575477855", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ Now, this is a benchmark that aligns with real world usage", "url": "https://x.com/JohnShina91/status/2117318565300961615"}, {"author_id": "2100385329824116736", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:05:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117317261501292828"], "id": "2117317261501292828", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117075900575477855", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ The 12% top score tells the real story — these tasks are genuinely hard, not benchmark-saturated. Great to see a frontier-level benchmark that actually stays ahead of the curve.", "url": "https://x.com/qihanblmg/status/2117317261501292828"}, {"author_id": "3061522932", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:00:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117315805532528807"], "id": "2117315805532528807", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117075900575477855", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ Which of the 11 domains has desk-ready headroom this week — coding or research?", "url": "https://x.com/hanrilaw/status/2117315805532528807"}], "includes": {"media": [{"height": 2074, "media_key": "3_2117075897945665537", "type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HWFdT_uXsAEzYJg.jpg", "width": 2162}, {"height": 1524, "media_key": "3_2117075897408761856", "type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HWFdT9uXMAAHhqG.jpg", "width": 2882}], "tweets": [{"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2117075897945665537"]}, "author_id": "1745106082790318080", "created_at": "2026-11-02T02:06:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117075900575477855"], "id": "2117075900575477855", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1287, "impression_count": 1521469, "like_count": 3111, "quote_count": 422, "reply_count": 332, "retweet_count": 300}, "text": "Today we’re releasing GDPx, a benchmark for measuring agentic capabilities across the most valuable domains.\n\nGDPx is a true frontier-level benchmark: even the best model scores just 12% (1/7)🧵 https://t.co/RNnkcuUkih"}, {"author_id": "806144160436809728", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:45:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117402764938756446"], "id": "2117402764938756446", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1745106082790318080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 13, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117075900575477855", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SemiAnalysis_ @grok The cost of Carbon is the actual api pricing or the temporary introductory pricing?"}, {"author_id": "471997769", "created_at": "2026-11-02T10:39:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117204917144170915"], "id": "2117204917144170915", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1963002119918620672", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 30, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117202353577148835", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@Balabo111 @damao